<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  robot_arm.urdf - ROS 2 description of the Universo 6-DOF arm (3-DOF arm; the gripper is one rigid link here).
  Generated from the Onshape export "Robot_ArmNew" of 30 Oct 2026 (onshape-to-robot). CAD links, meshes,
  mesh origins and inertials are copied verbatim; only the mesh paths and the joint frames changed.
  See ../URDF_CHANGES.md.

  Frames (REP-103):
   base_link : on the base yaw axis, at the base-plate part origin. x forward (direction the arm reaches at
               base_joint = 0), y left (along the shoulder axis), z up.
   arm_tip   : centre of the gripper mounting face (gripper base-plate origin) = IK target.
               x = along the forearm extrusion (outward), y = left, z = x cross y.

  Joint conventions:
   base_joint     : continuous (slip ring). + = counter-clockwise seen from above.
   shoulder_joint : 0 = upper arm (shoulder axis -> elbow axis line) vertical; negative = leaning forward.
                    Upper-arm elevation = 90 deg + q_shoulder.
   elbow_joint    : 0 = arm straight (elbow -> arm_tip line in line with the upper arm); + = forearm folds down.
                    Forearm (elbow -> arm_tip line) elevation = 90 deg + q_shoulder - q_elbow.
                    Elbow inner angle = 180 deg - q_elbow.
   Export joint values: l1End = q_shoulder - (-11.303 deg), L2 = q_elbow - (133.388 deg).

  Geometry (base_link, mm):
   shoulder axis : x 103.1763, z 64.5001
   shoulder -> elbow axis : 549.6141
   elbow axis -> arm_tip  : 476.6496 (in the arm plane)
   arm centre plane       : y = -1.9990 (arm_tip is this far to the side of the yaw axis at base_joint = 0)
   forearm extrusion is 5.2960 deg from the elbow -> arm_tip line
   upper-arm extrusion is -1.3029 deg from the shoulder -> elbow line

  Limits (Onshape mate limits: l1End -70..0 deg, L2 -120.104..0 deg):
   shoulder_joint : [-81.303, -11.303] deg  (upper-arm elevation 8.697 .. 78.697 deg)
   elbow_joint    : [13.284, 133.388] deg  (elbow inner angle 46.612 .. 166.716 deg)
   Shoulder/elbow effort and velocity are carried over from the previous model (the export has placeholders 10 / 10).
-->
